Found during k39: the merge goes through a Go map, so comments are dropped and keys re-sorted; only the first .bak keeps them (later runs do not back up again). A merge on yaml.v3 nodes would keep them. Also: hermesConfigMarker writes "do not edit" at the top of the whole user config, not just the unreagent block, which is misleading. Minor: a generated token is persisted to unreagent.local.yaml before the Hermes config is checked, so it stays when the merge refuses (harmless, the next run reuses it). Lane: unreagent-worker. Size M.


