2. hermes.go:351/447: an anchored mcp_servers (`mcp_servers: &srv` plus `backup_servers: *srv`) is extended in place, so every alias gains the unreagent entry too. That is the reason the alias case is refused (:361), so refuse this mirror case the same way, or document it. k39 changed only mcp_servers.
3. hermes.go:310-312: yaml.v3 v3.0.1 rewrites every merge key in the file as `!!merge <<:`, on lines outside the entry. The output is still valid YAML for PyYAML and yaml.v3, but it contradicts "the rest of the config stays as written". Clearing Tag "!!merge" on scalar nodes before encoding gives a plain `<<:` again (checked in a scratch copy).
4. hermes.go:142 + 494-513: writeFileAtomic is new for local.yaml. Fix or document each part. (a) A symlinked unreagent.local.yaml becomes a regular file, and the shared target does not get the token. k39 followed the symlink. For the Hermes config this predates k96 (k39 and 0.0.9 did the same). filepath.EvalSymlinks before temp+rename would fix both files. (b) An existing 0644 local.yaml ends up 0600 (k39 kept the mode). Arguably better for a file holding a token, but document it. (c) A read-only project directory with a writable local.yaml is now refused (fail-closed, nothing written; k39 succeeded).

